WEBVTT

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:04.150
What has happened to Kio-kun, the high school student?

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:06.620
Having arrived at his school on a small island south of Japan,

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:08.940
he discovered an extremely peculiar pot.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:15.630
Out of it, with a beautiful puff of smoke, appeared the incredibly cute alien Eris!

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.540
She finally managed to get close to Kio-kun, promising to stay by his side no matter what.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:25.750
How can an alien get everything she wants with just a single cute wink?!

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:30.000
What on Earth will happen to them?!

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.600
There are many new experiences,

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:45.440
yet there are varieties of answers right under our noses.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:52.490
How many pieces can the vast sky be split into?

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:54.320
Please give your whole self to me because I enjoy being with you.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.280
I don't really like sharing my fun.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.620
How I truly feel slips out under this blue sky...

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:00.660
Jeez!

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.530
I'll write out my name for you,

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:07.110
so that I will never fade from your memories.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:09.110
Why won't you be serious about me?

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:14.510
I won't let you take no for an answer.

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:21.180
Let's set up the cupid device and flick it on.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:25.110
We're driving on a runway full of impatience and dreams,

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:29.100
so tighten your seat belt and hold on tight.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:35.940
Let's back up our love and turn on a newer device.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:40.060
When it comes to your heart,

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:43.740
I only want the real one.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:47.700
I've come up with a plan to make you mine.

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:05.100
Come and Play

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:12.690
This is Coccoroco House, a certain restaurant in Okinawa City.

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:19.750
They are well known for their superb roast chicken, based on South American-style cuisine.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:24.950
Reserved Today!

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:24.950
Reserved?!

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:29.750
Oh, come on! You're hanging on to it, aren't you?

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:31.880
I'm not doing anything!

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:34.750
Who's holding on to the six of hearts?!

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:39.510
What, it's just you guys? Ah, count me in.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.760
One small plate with extra rice, okay?

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:47.040
Man, looks like you're all having a good time together.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:47.770
Ah!

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:56.990
*gulp*

00:02:58.350 --> 00:02:59.280
What's up?

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:02.780
It's nothing! Just a game!

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.700
Oh?

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:08.040
For "just a game", it seems a little serious to me.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.450
Well...

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:19.670
*cough*

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:21.400
Hm? What?

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.470
Oh! Ah!

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.970
"It all began this morning."

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:36.710
Thirty-four types of tiles multiplied by four each, for a total of 136.

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:43.680
From that, subtract fourteen and you get three trillion possible combinations.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:51.870
A social, competitive game where you try to win by collecting one of those specific combinations.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:56.880
<i>Hanchan</i>, a zero-sum game where you compete for points in each round.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:02.880
In many cases, a strategy of trying not to lose is more effective than trying to win... There!

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:10.560
Reading your opponent's hand through their discards while controlling yours to make it unreadable is important as well.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:16.610
Being able to talk during the game is also an excellent communication tool.

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:20.860
It's a surprisingly complex pastime, isn't it? <i>Riichi</i>!

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:21.860
<i>Ron</i>!

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.100
Huh?

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.160
Tada!

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:26.160
Big Three Dragons?!

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.080
And I'm the dealer, too!

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:30.710
A direct hit by a <i>yakuman</i>?

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:33.410
We were playing with no point limits, but I'm still on the <i>dora</i>!

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:37.110
What's more, you split the wall, so you pay double points.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.360
What?!

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:40.590
Aw, come on...

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.680
How many?

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:47.910
Seriously, I just don't get this "strip if you lose" rule.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:52.760
What's more, these "mahjong clothes" seem awfully similar to school uniforms.

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:56.980
The rules Eris got together said this is the way it's done.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:58.760
Oh?

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:01.150
Seems like there's still some room for more research.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:03.860
If we keep at it, maybe we'll eventually catch on.

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:11.050
But I... don't have anything left to take off.

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:15.790
Catch! If you go into negative points, it says you have to put on that box.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:20.680
So, do you think Eris is making progress with her research?

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:23.800
She said that she was going to do a field study with Kio-chi and the others today.

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.050
Field study?

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.800
(Sign) Coccoroco House

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.800
(Sign) Roast Chicken is our speciality!

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:44.770
The meat is so perfectly crisp, the garlic inside is so pungent and the flavour it adds to the meat is... Ah!

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:47.010
I'm so happy-so happy I could die!

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:48.810
Right, right, right.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:50.360
Anyway, what was today's business?

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:52.540
Something about helping with research, was it?

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:54.910
Ah! Ah awnt ooh o ewp...

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:56.990
Swallow first, then speak.

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:02.620
The truth is, Eris said she wanted to investigate human pastimes.

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:04.800
Investigate pastimes?

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:08.950
Yep!

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:14.620
I systematised and classified human pastimes as part of studying their culture and customs,

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:17.940
but I thought I had to try many things before I understood,

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:20.980
so maybe I could get all of you to help.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:25.350
Gotcha. With something like that, the more the merrier, right?

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:28.240
But why here at a restaurant?

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:32.430
If we're going to play a game together, I thought we would like to invite Antonia,

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:35.870
since she doesn't seem to have played games much before.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:40.750
Since it was an invitation from Eris-sama, I wanted to eat with her!

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:46.530
We found this restaurant when we lodged near here before, and our mistress has grown to trust them.

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:48.260
We have since become patrons here.

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:50.440
Oh?

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:54.760
Anyway, I gathered some seemingly team-oriented stuff.

00:06:55.180 --> 00:07:00.270
Mahjong, playing cards, flower cards, backgammon, chess, shogi, pop-up pirate and alligators!

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:03.110
Really? That sounds fun!

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:05.650
Just this kind of thing won't do, though.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:09.890
Playing games like this for research won't be any fun, you know.

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:15.600
It'd be no different from just reading the rule book.

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:19.040
With that, you'll never understand the true essence of leisure.

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:22.670
Well, what do you suggest?

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.670
The winners have to get prizes, of course.

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:28.550
Prizes?

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:29.710
Of course!

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:34.250
If there's a prize, people will really put their hearts into the competition and have a good time!

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:36.490
But what do we use for prizes?

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:38.680
You invited me, didn't you?

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.790
I'll provide the prizes.

00:07:53.980 --> 00:07:55.070
No good?

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:00.450
How about I go to the Swiss bank and get my name brand-

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:02.210
Wait! There's no need for that!

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:04.330
With this much, you can't really call it a game any more!

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:05.670
I see.

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:08.170
What should we do, then?

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:11.340
Mistress. How is this?

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:20.870
The Nekomimi Kyoudan, a portrait sculpture by the Kitten Paw.

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:25.350
It was requested by Nararl Genkeisha, and is a one-of-a-kind, highly sought-after item.

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:30.860
I'm not sure how I'd feel about getting a figurine of Eris.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:33.210
It doesn't suit your taste?

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:35.610
How would you find this, then?

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:43.870
An independent film produced the other day by the film and photography club.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:47.060
What? Don't you have anything better?!

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:51.380
Oh! That's the one I helped film!

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:56.160
It had shots of Kio-san sleeping peacefully, Kio-san eating a snack,

00:08:56.160 --> 00:09:03.770
Kio-san laughing, Kio-san failing and crying-all sorts of shots of Kio-san!

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:04.440
What?!

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:09.290
It had lots of shots of you changing, too!

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:12.710
I don't remember that!

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:15.700
All right, it's decided! This is the prize, okay?

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:17.950
Wait, Manami-chan!

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:20.290
Such bad manners.

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:23.700
What's wrong? It's not like watching it will do any harm!

00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:26.710
Kio-kun changing!

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:29.210
(Sign) Chastity Crisis

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:31.690
I can't just take from the others.

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:36.360
Maybe the Catian Embassy should prepare a prize, too.

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:41.470
What are these?

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:47.470
A three-piece set of chocolate wildcats from Iriomote that Kio-san gave to me!

00:09:47.470 --> 00:09:49.980
Uh... that's it?

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:53.230
It's secret and apparently very valuable!

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:56.770
No one's going to get excited about a prize like that!

00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:01.990
(Sign) Delivery for you

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:04.390
Oh, a delivery?

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:14.130
It seems to be a DVD.

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:17.130
It's Aoi-san and Manami-san!

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:22.470
"A real, naughty battle between two young women!"

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:27.660
"A hardcore, full-course feast of hot female action, Series 7."

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:31.870
"The Bunny Amazon from Hell versus The Dirty Slave Maid."

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:33.760
"Directed by Kawasaki Takao."

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:36.250
"Lead roles by Kinjou Manami, Futaba Aoi..."

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:37.180
That isn't...

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:38.820
No way! That's from-

00:10:39.590 --> 00:10:45.420
The two of them shot the film as part of the condition to borrow a powerboat.

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:53.840
At the request of "Dancer in the Dark", the manager of Las Pontelier, several cameras were hidden within the boat.

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:57.090
That bastard!

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:05.100
"Thanks to your help, I was able to complete the film."

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:10.660
"Please enjoy this sample. From Kawasaki Takao."

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:12.580
Wow, this is incredible!

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:18.240
Catia will contribute this as their prize, then!

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:19.740
Agreed!

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:21.240
(Sign) show me, show me

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:21.240
(Sign) I want to see

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:21.240
(Sign) I agree

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:22.300
But that...

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:24.280
Wait, you can't watch that!

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:26.930
What's wrong? It's not like watching it will do any harm!

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:32.000
You put up an embarrassing DVD of me as a prize, so we'll call this even.

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:40.260
And if we choose this as a prize, it seems the two of you will try even harder.

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:40.260
Mhm.

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:46.930
All right! With this, we've got all the prizes gathered.

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:49.780
If you have something you want, win it through the games!

00:11:57.600 --> 00:11:59.230
Now I get it.

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:01.950
That's why you're so serious.

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.990
It really is interesting, though!

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:08.440
When you add strategy to the element of chance, you can't win just by drawing the best hand.

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:10.010
It's a surprisingly complex game!

00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:13.020
Who's holding on to the six of hearts?!

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:17.200
Without it, we'll get nowhere! Six!

00:12:17.450 --> 00:12:18.210
(Sign) Yes?

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:24.970
I wasn't talking about you!

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:44.320
Royal straight flush.

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:46.070
What?!

00:12:47.020 --> 00:12:49.830
Looks the Doctor wins again.

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:52.830
People who can keep a straight face are hard to beat.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:56.830
Apparently, here on Earth they call that a "poker face"!

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:59.840
What an interesting game this is.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:02.590
I don't get why you have to strip if you lose, but...

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:06.340
Maybe if we keep at it, we'll eventually get it.

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:10.200
All right! Let's strip the Doctor down to nothing and make her all embarrassed and stuff!

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:15.600
Hope you're ready for it, really ready for it, you summer vegetable!

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:18.350
You'll only lose again.

00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:27.860
The girls are starting to catch on to the game.

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:37.790
On the other hand, Eris and the others are engaged in a fierce battle of Doubt with puns.

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:37.790
TL Note: Doubt is a Japanese card game similar to Bullshit.

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:59.350
TL Note: The following is a series of puns where the word includes the played number.

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:48.050
One, strawberry.

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:50.800
Two, carrot.

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:53.310
Three, policeman.

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:55.310
Four, Cro-Magnon.

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:57.560
Five, goronyan!

00:13:57.560 --> 00:13:59.350
Six, Rosin Bag.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:00.480
What's that?

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:02.930
Something that improves a pitcher's grip.

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:07.060
Well, whatever.

00:14:07.060 --> 00:14:10.990
Seven, "Just keep trying!"

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:11.830
Doubt!

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:15.020
See, I told you!

00:14:18.980 --> 00:14:20.290
I'm next, right?

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:22.860
Eight, long-legged wasp.

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:24.550
Nine, Tottori sand dunes!

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:27.050
Ten, veterinarian licence.

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:29.550
Eleven, Koizumi Juuichirou.

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:31.110
Twelve...

00:14:31.110 --> 00:14:32.300
Twelve...

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:34.510
Twelve...

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:35.990
Twelve Signs of the Zodiac!

00:14:35.990 --> 00:14:37.060
Doubt!

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:41.400
Oh, so <i>here's</i> the six of hearts!

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:46.110
Even with so many cards, you didn't have a twelve?

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:47.400
Shut up!

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:51.240
I tried so hard with my pun, too!

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:57.160
Manami-chan gets all shifty-eyed when she lies, doesn't she?

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:02.020
Thirteen, Thirteen Assassins.

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:04.370
One, Ichika-chan!

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:06.670
Two, paw pad.

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:08.220
Three, thank you!

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:09.090
Doubt!

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:15.560
Okay, Kio-chi wins!

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:17.180
Yay!

00:15:18.190 --> 00:15:23.560
All right, will the winner please pick one of the prizes.

00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:26.300
Hmm... Let's see...

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:27.820
Which one should I choose?

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:31.570
I really do want to see this DVD.

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:37.330
But I should absolutely get this back first.

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:43.640
This is no time to be feeling relieved!

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:46.670
We really wanted to see that movie, right?

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:48.130
That's not it!

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:50.800
Let us proceed to the next game.

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:01.020
The next method of competition will be...

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.770
*gulp*

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:06.570
Next, I want to try shooting something like this!

00:16:07.180 --> 00:16:09.510
Is this... sci-fi?

00:16:09.510 --> 00:16:12.700
It's kind of sci-fi, kind of fantasy.

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:16.320
Aliens come and fight each other!

00:16:16.800 --> 00:16:19.220
I've started watching that sort of thing recently.

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:23.830
Since it's an independent film, it might be better to go with a more original idea.

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:32.230
Since aliens don't necessarily look like humans, they could be based on a different form of DNA,

00:16:32.230 --> 00:16:35.310
or instead of being carbon-based, they could be silicon-based lifeforms,

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:39.020
or plasmic lifeforms that live on the surface of the sun!

00:16:39.020 --> 00:16:41.600
There are lots of unusual ideas you could run with!

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:47.150
But that's not realistic.

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:48.520
Not realistic?!

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:50.780
It's unscientific.

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:52.530
Unscientific?!

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:55.200
You've got to see the real thing to understand, right?

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:56.280
Right?

00:16:56.280 --> 00:17:00.860
When you imagine aliens, you imagine someone like Eris, right?

00:17:00.860 --> 00:17:02.140
Right!

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:07.930
Will science fiction ever recover from the damage?

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:12.050
Hey, everyone! Doing well?

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:16.200
Ah, Miyagi-san! Kakazu-kun isn't here today.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:19.420
No problem. Today, I didn't come for Kio.

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:22.010
I have business with these two.

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:25.650
Thanks for waiting!

00:17:25.650 --> 00:17:27.780
Yay!

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:39.070
(Sign) Family Restaurant Coccoroco House

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:39.070
(Sign) Roast Chicken

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:39.070
(Sign) Okinawa Soba

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:35.080
I'm going to get the railway and get rent from the bank!

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:35.830
Okay.

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:38.350
I want my land! I won the auction.

00:17:38.350 --> 00:17:39.070
Okay.

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:42.330
I'm going to build a hotel and buy the electric company.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:43.320
Okay.

00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:45.810
I object; I'm the judge!

00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:46.810
Okay.

00:17:46.810 --> 00:17:49.080
I don't have any more money!

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:54.320
With that, everyone's bankrupt.

00:17:54.320 --> 00:17:56.130
Antonia-san wins!

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:57.090
Of course I do!

00:17:57.090 --> 00:18:00.340
This is a game that's supposed to model a capitalistic society, right?

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:02.630
Just what you'd expect from the head of a big corporation.

00:18:02.630 --> 00:18:04.930
She's just too good with money.

00:18:06.720 --> 00:18:10.190
All right, will the winner please pick one of the prizes.

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:12.650
Let's see...

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:14.190
I want all of them, but...

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:16.190
*gulp*

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:19.950
I guess I'll reclaim my figurine!

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:24.950
Are you sure about that, Mistress?

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:27.460
I would hate to let it go.

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:30.060
We're safe!

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:32.660
The only things left are the chocolate cats and that DVD.

00:18:32.660 --> 00:18:35.990
If we lose the next one, someone's going to get that DVD!

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:39.120
Let us proceed to the next game.

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:41.470
The next method of competition will be...

00:18:45.710 --> 00:18:46.980
T-This is...!

00:19:04.220 --> 00:19:07.000
You were careless. Check.

00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:18.530
What?! I take back my move!

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:24.010
Fine!

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:29.270
If I am fairly beaten in a fight I put my heart into, I will admit defeat.

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:35.270
However, I will not leave defeated! Rematch!

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:47.230
Okay! Manami-chan's next!

00:19:47.230 --> 00:19:49.100
Right foot, red!

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:54.920
I'm going to fall!

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:57.210
Don't move, Manami-chan!

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:03.400
Next, Kio-chi! Right hand, blue!

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:07.310
What? Right hand on blue?

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:10.230
Here we go.

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:12.730
Where do you think you're sticking your face into?!

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:17.980
P-Please don't look!

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:20.240
Sorry!

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:26.170
Right! Next, Eris! Bonus!

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:27.970
Anything you want to yellow!

00:20:27.970 --> 00:20:29.310
Okay!

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:33.140
What's up with that?

00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:35.500
You can't do that, Eris! It has to be a hand or a foot!

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:37.890
But she said anything I want.

00:20:37.890 --> 00:20:39.700
That's against the rules!

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:41.760
The rest of us don't have tails!

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:43.350
Oh... I see.

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:45.890
Well, then, here I go!

00:20:48.130 --> 00:20:52.140
Hey, what do you think you're doing, moving like that?!

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:55.150
But Manami-san said...

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:57.400
Whatever, just get off me!

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:59.150
But...

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:01.650
What? What's going on?

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:05.320
Fine, you can use your tail! Just get <i>off</i>!

00:21:06.430 --> 00:21:09.080
All right, then.

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:19.840
Okay! Eris wins!

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:25.340
Um... Let's see...

00:21:26.920 --> 00:21:29.350
I'll go with this!

00:21:32.160 --> 00:21:33.420
Are you sure about that?

00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:37.850
Yep! After all, I got these from Kio-san, so they're important.

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:41.920
This is bad for my heart.

00:21:42.510 --> 00:21:44.400
Yeah. The DVD is all that's left, right?

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:47.610
This is it. We can't lose again!

00:21:48.110 --> 00:21:50.760
Let us proceed to the next game.

00:21:55.870 --> 00:21:58.060
The next method of competition will be...

00:21:58.880 --> 00:22:00.380
*gulp*

00:22:00.890 --> 00:22:02.130
Strip Baseball Rock-Paper-Scissors!

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:05.880
Out! Safe! Here we go!

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:08.890
Argh! I lost again?!

00:22:09.310 --> 00:22:12.190
Not too good at rock-paper-scissors, are you, Doctor?

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:16.390
I can't stand thoughtless games of chance like this...

00:22:16.390 --> 00:22:19.500
Oh, but it isn't all mindless!

00:22:19.500 --> 00:22:22.150
There's some strategy in what you pick each round.

00:22:22.150 --> 00:22:27.650
It's odd that... all human games seem to involve betting your clothing.

00:22:27.650 --> 00:22:31.050
It's probably a relic from before they had money.

00:22:31.050 --> 00:22:34.330
All right! Let's strip the Doctor naked!

00:22:35.660 --> 00:22:39.170
Out! Safe! Here we go!

00:22:39.740 --> 00:22:42.170
Which one is it? Did I win?

00:22:42.170 --> 00:22:45.630
Yeah, yeah, you won. Shut up!

00:22:46.310 --> 00:22:48.380
I have to take this off, too?

00:22:48.870 --> 00:22:51.140
Yep, that's the rule.

00:22:51.710 --> 00:22:53.430
I lost as well.

00:22:53.840 --> 00:22:56.470
Kio's really good, even with his eyes covered!

00:22:56.950 --> 00:23:01.560
No, it's more like he's able to focus even more with his eyes covered.

00:23:02.010 --> 00:23:05.150
All right, there goes the last layer!

00:23:05.150 --> 00:23:06.400
Here I come!

00:23:06.400 --> 00:23:10.660
Out! Safe! Here we go!

00:23:14.820 --> 00:23:17.660
Kio-san won the last one, too!

00:23:18.870 --> 00:23:20.670
Fine. I'm taking it off, okay?

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:22.670
To be defeated in each round...

00:23:22.670 --> 00:23:24.420
I am ashamed.

00:23:24.420 --> 00:23:25.920
I tried so hard, too...

00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:28.420
The competitive world is so harsh, isn't it?

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:31.180
All right, I'm going to take this one off.

00:23:31.180 --> 00:23:33.140
That's unfair! What's up with that?

00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:35.020
One layer is one layer.

00:23:35.020 --> 00:23:36.700
That's playing dirty!

00:23:36.700 --> 00:23:40.060
Complain to the rule book, then.

00:23:40.060 --> 00:23:42.560
No way! Give up and take it off!

00:23:42.560 --> 00:23:44.140
Stop it!

00:23:44.140 --> 00:23:46.520
What are you doing to the Mistress?

00:23:46.520 --> 00:23:48.940
What? What's going on?

00:23:46.520 --> 00:23:47.810
Get back!

00:23:48.570 --> 00:23:49.600
Give that to me!

00:23:49.600 --> 00:23:50.640
Let go!

00:23:58.700 --> 00:23:59.770
Ow...

00:24:17.800 --> 00:24:21.630
The winner will receive the final prize.

00:24:24.260 --> 00:24:32.090
Such a lucky winner! Since you tried so hard, I will now give this to you!

00:24:32.090 --> 00:24:33.360
Thank you!

00:24:38.500 --> 00:24:39.860
What do we do now?

00:24:39.860 --> 00:24:41.870
If Kio-kun watches that...

00:24:41.870 --> 00:24:42.910
Here!

00:24:45.450 --> 00:24:47.120
You wanted this, didn't you?

00:24:47.120 --> 00:24:49.630
Yeah, but...

00:24:49.630 --> 00:24:51.420
Is it okay, Kio-kun?

00:24:51.750 --> 00:24:54.790
It's a movie <i>you</i> filmed, after all.

00:24:54.790 --> 00:24:57.180
You should be the first to see it.

00:24:58.570 --> 00:24:59.870
Kio...

00:25:00.540 --> 00:25:01.930
Thank you!

00:25:01.930 --> 00:25:04.810
In exchange, you have to show it to me afterwards, okay?

00:25:05.140 --> 00:25:07.810
O-Okay.

00:25:09.790 --> 00:25:12.070
Human games are fun, aren't they?

00:25:12.070 --> 00:25:18.020
Right. Losing at times makes winning much more fun.

00:25:18.020 --> 00:25:21.830
Mistress... You've grown so much!

00:25:21.830 --> 00:25:23.170
Indeed.

00:25:23.170 --> 00:25:27.170
However, the crisis of Aoi and Manami is yet to be averted.

00:25:27.170 --> 00:25:28.840
Huh?

00:25:34.340 --> 00:25:36.780
There it is, Onee-sama!

00:25:37.490 --> 00:25:40.350
Okay, here goes nothing!

00:25:42.850 --> 00:25:44.860
Roar!

00:25:48.840 --> 00:25:50.860
Roar!

00:25:50.860 --> 00:25:52.860
Growl!

00:26:00.370 --> 00:26:04.350
The rocket launcher isn't working! What happened?!

00:26:04.350 --> 00:26:07.060
We'll have to fall back to our last resort!

00:26:09.630 --> 00:26:11.380
Roar! Roar!

00:26:15.130 --> 00:26:18.380
Hey, lookin' pretty good!

00:26:19.800 --> 00:26:23.530
Come on, say something about our voice acting, too!

00:26:23.530 --> 00:26:27.110
Sorry, sorry! You did really well!

00:26:27.110 --> 00:26:29.800
With something like this, you might be able to go professional!

00:26:29.800 --> 00:26:30.650
Really?!

00:26:31.410 --> 00:26:35.650
Get us another job from Director Kawasaki, then!

00:26:35.650 --> 00:26:40.160
Hey! Let's show this film at the culture festival!

00:26:40.160 --> 00:26:41.660
I agree!

00:26:42.490 --> 00:26:45.930
OUT OF THE QUESTION!

00:27:01.950 --> 00:27:04.070
If you'd like to see me, (Right away)

00:27:04.070 --> 00:27:07.060
I would like to run to you. (Of course)

00:27:07.060 --> 00:27:11.540
A friend is a treasure.

00:27:11.540 --> 00:27:13.720
And if you were to talk, (Somewhat)

00:27:13.720 --> 00:27:16.660
I'd listen to what upset you. (Which he forgets)

00:27:16.660 --> 00:27:21.430
I feel like laughing out loud.

00:27:21.430 --> 00:27:26.260
Riding on our heart's rhythm,

00:27:26.260 --> 00:27:29.500
we'll make peace signs to the blue sky.

00:27:30.460 --> 00:27:32.910
We'll walk together hand-in-hand, (Good)

00:27:32.910 --> 00:27:35.570
and our joy will go up. ↑ (More)

00:27:35.570 --> 00:27:40.240
I'll sing and sing loud...

00:27:40.920 --> 00:27:42.790
...right here.

00:27:42.790 --> 00:27:47.470
There's someone I love.

00:27:47.470 --> 00:27:52.420
Because it's "happiness",

00:27:52.420 --> 00:27:56.270
it will make your smile bloom.

00:27:56.270 --> 00:28:06.740
Let's dance! Look! Tomorrow is waiting.

00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:20.170
They're swinging!

00:28:19.570 --> 00:28:20.830
They're heavy!

00:28:20.170 --> 00:28:21.590
They're swinging, they're swinging!

00:28:20.840 --> 00:28:22.630
They're really heavy!

00:28:21.880 --> 00:28:23.260
Mine are also swinging!

00:28:23.900 --> 00:28:24.930
They <i>are</i> heavy, right?

00:28:29.310 --> 00:28:33.690
(sign) Next time, come and play! (Hopefully)

00:28:42.640 --> 00:28:49.790
(sign) Shinno Okina - Media Factory / Catia Embassy
